The semantics supports both string slicing and `zip`. I’m choosing a small recursive implementation that matches Python’s `zip` behavior—XOR the heads and stop when either input is exhausted—because its recursive structure gives the symbolic proof a clean induction over the two code sequences. The proof will cover arbitrary equal-or-unequal input lengths, with the bit-domain precondition from the prompt.
